    {
      "id": "AC1",
      "text": "A first starting value added to an empty shared world produces valid JSON and preserves false, null and the empty string as explicit values."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC2",
      "text": "Adding the first key to a nested empty object also keeps valid JSON, including when the key is `__proto__` or `constructor`."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC3",
      "text": "The surrounding scenario and the seed reference snapshot remain unchanged."
